PRE-TABLE AMENDMENT, PASS 11 -- its own file (mtime against part11/driver.log is the order witness).

SECTION 19 -- the generating set for the idata partitions at every pending cell, under the floor pass 11 bounded.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* THE RULING (fable5, the rule's own author, asked to be harder on it than anyone): the rule as written
  demanded all 128 body-tested cells and was #392-prone; the FLOOR is {dominating predicates} x {device-STATE
  lvalues the fix's repair path reads that are jointly reachable through its own data flow} = {label} x
  {p1} x {p2}, eight cells, all rowed by pass 10.  The tested bits of the written idata are single-operand
  MARGINALS -- clause-(e) debt.  Seven other seats split (codex/glm/minimax: the letter demands the
  remainder; grok: a generating set per axis; kimi-sub: feedback-edge partitions plus one witness;
  deepseek: narrow to guard predicates); the Opus seat MEASURED `&& !(p2 && (idata & ICLR))' on the
  203-row instrument (its result is in its findings).  ADJUDICATED: the bounded floor is adopted; the
  debt is taken as L1 construction with a measured warrant, in the generating-set form.
* THE GENERATING SET: at every rowed pending cell (pend2 at both labels, pend1 at both, pendboth at
  both) write each tested idata bit CLEAR and SET -- IEN already (0x0000 / 0x0013), now ICLR (0x0018 =
  IEN|ICLR) and the HUH? bits (0x0020) -- twelve wide writes APPENDED to the three sessions so the
  existing readback indices do not move, plus a `huh' row per session counting the HUH? print.
* LANDED VALUES (the preset-collision check): 0x0018 at an armed ICR (0x31, count 1) -> store 0x30, the
  strobe decrements the count to 0 and clears INT -> 0x10; at an idle ICR (0x11) -> 0x10.  0x0020 at an
  armed ICR -> 0x20 (IEN clear zeroes the count; INT kept; HUH? printed); at an idle one -> 0x00.  None
  equals a preset (0x11, 0x31) -- and 0x20 equals the landed-0x0000 value, which is why the `*h'
  readbacks alone would not separate M_HI from M_PENDBOTH: the `huh' rows do.
* THE FOUR MANDATED CHECKS (run, not asserted):
  - SIBLING PARITY -- at the shared block the siblings are the LABELS: every new write is made at BOTH
    labels in every timer session; the guest path (T2 only by construction) is disclosed as before.
  - CLAIM -> ROW -- "each tested idata bit written both clear and set at every pending cell" -> the `*i',
    `*c', `*h' readbacks (six per session); "a landed 0x0020 prints HUH?" -> the `huh' rows; "the floor is
    eight cells, all held" -> the pass-10 rows named cell by cell; "INT clear with a count pending is
    unreachable" -> no row, a DERIVATION (the tick increments only under IEN; reassert sets INT).
  - GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD -- unchanged from pass 10: the guard cannot see the counts, the label or
    the idata bits; the readbacks (and now the HUH? print) are the channel.
  - CHANNEL -- pend2 rbc <- M_ICLR (0x10 vs 0x31); pend2 rbh <- M_ICLR (0x10: declined after the
    decrement) and M_HI (0x20); pend2 huh <- M_HI (1 vs 0); pend2 rb1c / rb1h <- no mutant in this
    table (the (T1, 0, >0) ICLR/HI cells: M_P2T1-shaped joints with ICLR would red them; held for the
    generating set, said here); pend1 rbc / rbh / rb2c / rb2h <- M_P1IEN (0x10 / 0x10 / 0x13 / 0x13,
    through the landed 0x0013 and 0x0018 writes); pend1 huh <- none (the 0x0020 writes stay declined
    under all three: pend1's count is zeroed before its HUH write under M_P1IEN); pendboth rbc / rbh <-
    M_ICLR (0x10) and M_P1IEN (0x10); pendboth huh <- M_HI (1); pendboth rb1c / rb1h <- M_P1IEN (0x10).
    Rows with no mutant in this table: pend2 rb1c, pend2 rb1h, pend1 huh -- stated, not hidden.
* THE ORDER MATTERS UNDER A MUTANT: a landed 0x0018 decrements the count (1 -> 0) and a landed 0x0000 or
  0x0020 zeroes it, so a count-conditioned guard RE-ARMS for the later writes in the session; every
  prediction below derives the readbacks in session order.
* NOT hand-verified at writing: the twelve new shapes (the same instructions as the pass-10 ones with
  r11/r12); verified by BASE coming back full -- the driver ABORTS otherwise -- and by mut_syntax.py on
  the three mutant strings before the table.
PREDICTIONS for part 11 (three mutants plus BASE, 218-row instrument):
